    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Three-dimensional jagged array (where the number of columns can vary), implemented via an unordered_map plus hashing function &apos;<ref refid="structcsmp_1_1_tuple_hash" kindref="compound">TupleHash</ref>&apos; Tested and compared in &apos;<ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_jagged_array3_d___comparison___test" kindref="compound">JaggedArray3D_Comparison_Test</ref>&apos;. For dense regularly shaped matrix, <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_jagged_array3_d" kindref="compound">JaggedArray3D</ref> is slower than <ref refid="class_dynamic_array3_d" kindref="compound">DynamicArray3D</ref> and a vector of vecto of vectors. Good uses are for sparse 3D matrices the entries of which are in a flux (changing rapidly during a computation). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
